! GAMESS/VB2000 Test 39.
! This is an input file that been generated by a molden2gamess 
! program. There are several. This one differs in that it supplies
! the HF orbital energies (eigenvalues). The geometry, basis set 
! and HF orbitals are from the Molden file. Since we have the HF 
! orbitals, there is no need to calculate them in GAMESS. 
! Calculation of the HF orbitals is skipped using the $SKIPGMSHF 
! directive. The HF orbitals are read by the same code that $READMOS uses.
!
! Note that the $GUESS line in the data would not normally be needed,
! but changing GUESS=MOREAD to GUESS=SKIP skips the initial guess code,
! thus saving time and cutting output. It is of course generated by the
! molden2gamess scripts because the VEC group is normally used by GUESS.
!
! It is a SC run on benzene with the 6-31G* basis set, but the 5
! structures specified to get pure non-crossing Rumer structures.
!
! Thus file was created by molden2gmsvb.f which is in the vb2000/SRC/
! directory. If compiled to give molden2gmsvb.x, and put in your path,
! then running in the vb2000/tests directory:-
!    molden2gmsvb.x test_mol_for_39
! will give you test_mol_for_39.inp, which is the basis of this input
! file.
!
! Note the $EIGENVALUE block which allows all NBASIS number of orbital
! energies to be read. If this is absent, the orbital energies are all
! set to zero. This normally works OK, but it is good to have the 
! actual correct orbital energies.
!
 $CONTRL ISPHER=0 SCFTYP=RHF MULT=1
  UNITS=BOHR COORD=UNIQUE VBTYP=VB2000 $END
 $GUESS GUESS=SKIP $END
 $DATA
